      "text": "A knot is the simplest rope terminal but the most expensive in strength. A splice is the structurally superior alternative: it preserves 90–98% of rope breaking strength vs. a knot's 50–75%. Ashley's taxonomy provides the framework for understanding what every knot does and why it works."
